# D8  (was Q1) THE LOCKED EXIT STAYS IN THE ADAPTER as TIER 3 prose.
#     No terminal runbook, no new selector shape, no conclude/handoff output.
#     Owner's reasoning: if this programme succeeds, `/plan` gets the same
#     treatment, and the stage-to-stage handoff interface is better designed
#     once against two real cases than guessed at now against one.
#     RE-WARRANTED BY D13 — the ruling stands, the JUSTIFICATION narrows. The
#     Locked exit has the MOST PRECISE TRIGGER MOMENT IN THE WHOLE FILE: the
#     instant the run reaches terminal. So "no delivery moment could be located"
#     is emphatically NOT why it stays prose. The reason is DEFERRAL — we know
#     the moment and are declining to build the mechanism until a second case
#     shows what shape it wants. Legitimate, and a DIFFERENT warrant. Recorded
#     as DEFERRED AND KNOWN-WEAK, not as legitimately kept; the residue most
#     likely to be repaid first.
#
# D9  (was Q3) THE EIGHT GUARDRAILS ARE TRIAGED, NOT MOVED WHOLESALE — and the
#     triage is itself a DESIGN ACTIVITY, not a mechanical sort. Three buckets:
#     restates an engine invariant -> delete or fold into the sealed stage hymn;
#     is really a step at a specific moment -> assign an edge, make it a step;
#     genuinely ambient judgement -> TIER 3, and the adapter keeps it without
#     apology. This triage IS the `EN-2` (b) answer.
#
# D10 (was Q4) SELECTOR RECORDING — RULED "STAYS AS PROSE", THEN **REVERSED BY
#     D13**. It is now STEPS ON EDGES 3 AND 4.
#     The original ruling: this wants MORE THAN ONE hook across design and plan
#     — it is iterative, research can trigger it, a decision can trigger it —
#     and modelling it as a single step on one edge would be a worse lie than
#     prose, because a discharge asserts a completeness the obligation lacks.
#     UNPICKED, that objection has two parts and only one survives:
#       OVERCLAIMING IS A GENUINE HARM. "Record the design-target selectors",
#         discharged once, does assert the touch-set is settled when it is not.
#       MULTI-HOOK IS NOT THE HARM. It was carrying the original ruling, and
#         under D13 corollary (2) it argues the opposite way.
#     So the remedy is STEP TEXT THAT DOES NOT OVERCLAIM, not the absence of
#     delivery: "record the design-target selectors the code-impact section NOW
#     COMMITS TO" is true at each firing and asserts nothing about finality.
#     Edge 3 is where the code-impact section locks — exactly where the
#     incumbent prose says it fires; edge 4 is where review may have moved it.
#     RESIDUAL, still open: the hooks ACROSS DESIGN AND PLAN stay unmodelled,
#     because /plan has no runbook machinery yet. D13 makes that a known gap in
#     coverage rather than a warrant for delivering nothing at the two moments
#     we can already reach.
#
