#
#         THE ANOMALY CONTROL MOVES INTO THE FIRING CONDITION, where it can
#         be stated BEFORE any run rather than chosen after one. The signal
#         fires only when ALL hold: (a) the within-run sibling control is
#         satisfied; (b) the run did NOT cross a deliberate context break or
#         resume at that edge — CHR-049's protocol deliberately induces one,
#         which makes this identifiable rather than hypothetical; (c) the
#         run was not aborted or restarted mid-edge. [(b) WIDENED AND (d)
#         ADDED AT ROUND 7 — see the F-14/F-15 block below.]
#
#         THE ASYMMETRY IS DELIBERATE. Reword is the conservative arm and
