#
#     >>> AMENDED — RV-325 round 7, F-14 and F-15, owner ruling 2026-08-01.
#         SEVENTH INSTANCE OF THE PATTERN, AND ITS TWO FACES. The round-6
#         repair narrowed the EXIT SET and the EXCLUSION SET in one move,
#         and each narrowing lost something the thing it replaced covered.
#         That is why the two findings arrived together and why answering
#         them in sequence gives a wrong answer.
#
#         FACE ONE — THE EXIT SET (F-15). `Both revise the placement or its
#         boundary contract` is WITHDRAWN AS FALSE. Rewording a 2a step's
#         boundary text leaves it a 2a step on the same edge: it revises the
#         obligation's CONTRACT, not its PLACEMENT. The sentence broadened
#         VA-4's noun so the cheap arm would qualify — structurally what
#         `stand` was doing. Removing `stand` closed the zero-revision exit
#         and installed a NO-PLACEMENT-REVISION exit in its place.
#
#         VA-4 IS NOT AMENDED. It asks each signal to name A result that
#         would revise the placement, and RECLASSIFICATION is that result.
#         What defeats the criterion is not a cheap arm's presence but an
#         UNREACHABLE EXPENSIVE ONE. The repair goes to reachability.
#
#         THE REOPENING IS PRE-REGISTERED. Every other link in the chain was
#         — observation, sibling control, firing condition, resolution set —
#         and the CHOICE BETWEEN THE ARMS was left to `the reopening`, which
#         is route-to-the-cheapest-revision with the routing step renamed: a
#         VA-5 breach on its own terms. The rule: (1) RECLASSIFY TO 2b IS
#         THE DEFAULT; (2) REWORD MUST PRODUCE AN ARTEFACT — candidate step
#         text naming a completion boundary that is truthful AND observable
#         in run state at the moment it says the step completes, the same
#         standard signal (i) meets; no candidate text, no reword; (3)
#         REWORD IS ONE-SHOT PER STEP — a second firing on the same step
#         spends cause (C) and reclassifies. The cost gradient inverts: the
#         cheap arm costs a checkable artefact and failing to produce one
#         compels the expensive one. F-12's correction is untouched; nothing
#         reclassifies on the raw event, and cause (B) still routes to
#         adherence.
#
#         FACE TWO — THE EXCLUSION SET (F-14). `stand` covered ANOMALY,
#         unbounded. Its replacement covers three NAMED events and omits the
#         commonest: INCIDENTAL CONTEXT EXHAUSTION OR COMPACTION, which
#         nothing marks — CHR-049 records only `refresh and exact resume
#         across a deliberate context break`. A run can therefore satisfy
#         the written condition after an unmarked context loss.
#
#         THE RUN RECORD CANNOT CLOSE THIS. Doctrine observes writes, not an
#         agent's context — the limit already disclosed for IMP-373's
#         repayment signal. So of F-14's three remedies, bounding the
#         exercise is unverifiable in advance, a run-record proxy does not
