#         write and not CHR-049's (that chore's Boundary says so).
#
#         THE FIRING CONDITION BECOMES: (a) sibling control satisfied; (b)
#         NO CONTEXT BOUNDARY crossed at that edge — deliberate break or
#         resume, OR INCIDENTAL EXHAUSTION, COMPACTION OR HARNESS-INITIATED
#         SUMMARISATION; (c) no abort or restart mid-edge; (d) THE PROTOCOL
#         RECORDED THE CONTEXT STATE across the window containing the
#         discharge — absent that record (b) is UNDECIDED and the
#         observation is UNCOLLECTED, NOT WEIGHED, the disposal the sibling
#         control already takes. DEFAULT-DENY is what makes the condition
#         decidable: satisfied only on positive evidence, never by the
#         absence of a mark.
#
#         COST, DISCLOSED. Default-deny lowers the firing probability, and
#         at N=1 a falsifier that cannot fire is a formality. Recording
#         context boundaries is a standing moderator obligation with a named
#         field, so the deny branch should be rare — and if it is NOT rare
#         the kit must REPORT that, because a run whose context state went
#         unrecorded is evidence the exercise cannot support this signal.
#
#         THE ROUND-6 WARRANT LAPSES AND IS REPLACED, NOT RESTATED. `A
